# PowerShell Basics and File Management

## Overview
Today I explored the fundamentals of PowerShell, including cmdlets, aliases, help commands, module management, and file system navigation. I also learned how PowerShell uses an object-oriented approach instead of plain text processing.

---

# Topics Covered

## Introduction to PowerShell
- PowerShell is a task automation and configuration management tool by Microsoft
- Built on the .NET framework
- Uses an object-oriented approach
- Cross-platform support:
  - Windows
  - Linux
  - macOS

## History of PowerShell
- Created to overcome limitations of `cmd.exe` and batch scripting
- Developed by Jeffrey Snover
- Released in 2006
- PowerShell Core released in 2016

---

# PowerShell Objects
- PowerShell works with objects instead of plain text
- Objects contain:
  - Properties
  - Methods

### Example
- Car object:
  - Properties:
    - Color
    - FuelLevel
  - Methods:
    - Drive()
    - Refuel()

