# Launching PowerShell

## Start PowerShell from CMD
```powershell
powershell
```

- `PS` indicates PowerShell shell

---

# Cmdlets

## Verb-Noun Syntax
- PowerShell commands are called cmdlets
- Follow `Verb-Noun` naming format

### Examples
```powershell
Get-Content
Set-Location
```

---

# Important Cmdlets

## Get-Command
- Lists available cmdlets and functions

```powershell
Get-Command
```

### Filter Functions
```powershell
Get-Command -CommandType Function
```

---

## Get-Help
- Displays cmdlet help information

```powershell
Get-Help Get-Date
```

### Extra Help Options
```powershell
Get-Help Get-Date -examples
Get-Help Get-Date -detailed
Get-Help Get-Date -full
Get-Help Get-Date -online
```

